Privacy Policy

Supermarket Boss: Tycoon · Vainsteel Studios · Last updated: October 20, 2026

Short version. Supermarket Boss: Tycoon has no accounts and no sign-up. We, the developer, do not collect your name, email address, phone number or precise location, and we do not run our own servers. Your progress is saved on your device. Ads, in-app purchases and the optional cloud save are handled by Google and Apple, which process limited data under their own privacy policies.

Who we are
Supermarket Boss: Tycoon (Android package / iOS bundle ID: com.vainsteel.supermarket) is developed and published by Vainsteel Studios. This policy applies to the Android version distributed on Google Play and the iOS/iPadOS version distributed on the Apple App Store.

Information stored on your device
The game saves your progress locally on your device using standard app storage. This includes:
game state — cash, gold, stores, shelves and their layout, staff, upgrades, research, quests, league progress and achievements;
preferences — language, sound, music, vibration and zoom settings;
purchase flags — whether you own the Starter Pack or the Supporter Pack, and whether end-of-day ads are removed.
This data stays on your device. We do not upload it to our own servers and we cannot read it. Uninstalling the game or clearing its data deletes it.

Optional cloud save (Android only)
On Android you can choose to connect the game to Google Play Games Services ("Cloud Save" in Settings). If you do, a copy of your game save is stored in the Saved Games area of your own Google Play Games account so that you can restore it on another device. This copy contains only the game data listed in section 2. It is stored and protected by Google under the Google Privacy Policy; we cannot access your Google account. You can delete Play Games data at any time from the Google Play Games app or your Google Account settings. The iOS version does not use any cloud save service.

Advertising
The game is free and supported by ads served through Google AdMob, including optional rewarded ads that you choose to watch in exchange for in-game bonuses, and occasional end-of-day ads.
To serve and measure ads, Google may process:
your device's advertising identifier (Android Advertising ID, or Apple IDFA on iOS — only if you allow tracking);
coarse technical information such as device model, operating system version, language and approximate region derived from your IP address;
ad interaction data, such as whether an ad was shown, viewed or clicked.
We do not receive, store or sell this data.
Consent. Users in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are shown Google's consent form before personalised ads are used, and can change their choice at any time under Settings → Privacy options in the game.

iOS App Tracking Transparency. On iOS, the game asks for your permission before the advertising identifier (IDFA) may be used for tracking. If you choose "Ask App Not to Track", only non-personalised or contextual ads are shown. You can change this at any time in iOS Settings → Privacy & Security → Tracking.
Any purchase in the game permanently removes end-of-day ads. Rewarded ads remain optional.
Learn more: Google Privacy Policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy) and How Google uses information from apps that use its services (https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites).

In-app purchases
The game offers optional in-app purchases (gold packs, Piggy Bank, Starter Pack, Supporter Pack). Purchases are processed entirely by Google Play Billing on Android and by the Apple App Store on iOS. We never see or store your payment card, billing address or store account details; the store only tells the game whether a purchase was completed, which the game records locally. Purchases are subject to the Google Play Terms of Service or Apple's Media Services Terms. Non-consumable purchases (Starter Pack, Supporter Pack) can be restored at any time via Settings → Restore Purchases.

Notifications
With your permission, the game schedules local reminders on your device (for example, when a seasonal event starts or a daily reward is ready). These are created on the device itself; no personal data is sent to us or to a push-notification server. You can turn them off in your device's notification settings.

Permissions
The game uses internet access to load ads, process purchases and (on Android, if you choose) sync your cloud save. It does not access your contacts, camera, microphone, photos, files or precise location.

Children
The game is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information to a third-party service through this game, please contact us and we will help you reach the relevant provider.

Data sharing and retention
We do not sell, rent or trade any information, and we do not hold personal data on our own servers. The only processing is carried out by Google (AdMob, Play Billing, Play Games Services) and Apple (App Store) under their own policies. Because we keep no personal data, there is nothing for us to retain, export or erase on your behalf; you stay in control:
Erase game data — uninstall the game or clear its data.
Erase cloud save (Android) — delete it from Google Play Games / your Google Account.
Limit ad personalisation — use Settings → Privacy options in the game, reset your advertising ID (Android) or disable tracking (iOS).
Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR or the CCPA), you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data held about you; for data processed by Google or Apple, please use their tools, and contact us if you need help.

Security
We take reasonable measures to protect the game. However, no method of electronic storage or transmission is completely secure.

Changes to this policy
If this policy changes, the updated version will be published at this address and the "Last updated" date above will change.

